    "created_at": "2026-10-06T17:51:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-06T17:51:56Z",
    "body": "I checked. For U+0000 to U+007F plus U+0080, U+00A0, U+00AD, U+00E9, U+2028, U+2029, U+FEFF, U+FFFD and U+1F600, each at the start, in the middle and at the end of `a=b` (411 inputs), I compared `[...url.searchParams]` after `url.search = input`, both untouched and with `url.searchParams` read first, in Chrome 154, Chromium 153, Firefox 155, WebKit 26.6, Node.js 26 and whatwg-url 17.2.0.\n\nTab, LF and CR are the only inputs where the list differs, between implementations or between the two cases in Chromium. `a b` gives `[[\"a b\", \"\"]]` everywhere; the query becomes `a%20b`, which decodes back to the same list. Those three are the code points the URL parser removes outright, and they are the only inputs I tried where parsing `url.search` back gives a different list from parsing the raw input.\n\nIn Chromium, the read-first case matches parsing the raw input on all 411 inputs, and the untouched case matches Firefox, WebKit and Node.js on all 411.\n",
